{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/469", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Lets write book on \\\"Delaware C Corp for Non-US Solo Founder\\\". \\nI want to cover all important topics. important topics are - incorporation and various complaince. Basically this book will help non US solo Founders to run and operate a Delaware C Corp easily using various services. This book should be GoTo manual for all help needed to effecting run and operate Delaware C Corp.\\n\\nSince book will be long. I want you to first give me Table of Content. TOC will consist of Chaters and Sections. \\nOnce you reply me the TOC, I will ask one by one like - for example \\\"chapter 2, section 5\\\" like that, and you will reply me that section. This way, we can produce this book. Are you ready.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here's a suggested table of content for the book:\\n\\nChapter 1: Introduction to Delaware C Corp for Non-US Solo Founder\\n\\n    1.1. What is a Delaware C Corp?\\n    1.2. Why choose a Delaware C Corp for a non-US solo founder?\\n    1.3. Who is this book for?\\n\\nChapter 2: Incorporation of a Delaware C Corp\\n\\n    2.1. Choosing a business name\\n    2.2. Filing articles of incorporation\\n    2.3. Obtaining a federal tax ID number\\n    2.4. Setting up a corporate bank account\\n\\nChapter 3: Compliance Requirements for a Delaware C Corp\\n\\n    3.1. Annual report filing\\n    3.2. Annual meeting of shareholders\\n    3.3. Minutes of board of directors meetings\\n    3.4. Filing tax returns\\n    3.5. Maintaining corporate records\\n\\nChapter 4: Operating a Delaware C Corp\\n\\n    4.1. Issuing shares of stock\\n    4.2. Hiring employees or contractors\\n    4.3. Paying salaries or dividends\\n    4.4. Closing down a corporation\\n\\nChapter 5: Using Services to Manage a Delaware C Corp\\n\\n    5.1. Choosing a registered agent\\n    5.2. Using a corporate service provider\\n    5.3. Using a virtual office service\\n    5.4. Using a bookkeeping or accounting service\\n\\nChapter 6: Common Issues for Non-US Solo Founders\\n\\n    6.1. Foreign investment restrictions\\n    6.2. Tax implications for non-US citizens\\n    6.3. Legal requirements for operating a business abroad\\n    6.4. Protecting intellectual property rights\\n\\nChapter 7: Conclusion\\n\\n    7.1. Key takeaways\\n    7.2. Final thoughts\\n\\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any questions or if there's anything specific you'd like me to cover in more detail.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/7", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"some people appear with excessive fashion or overly exposed body to show off. when i hang with someone like this, what kind of joke can i make?\", \"response\": \"There are a few different approaches you can take when making a joke about someone's excessive fashion or body exposure. Here are a few examples:\\n\\n1. Play on the absurdity of it all: You could make a joke about how over-the-top their outfit is, or how much skin they're showing. For example, you could say something like, \\\"Wow, you must have really wanted to stand out today!\\\" or \\\"I didn't know you were planning on going to the beach, too!\\\"\\n\\n2. Make a lighthearted joke about the trend: If their fashion or exposure is following a particular trend, you could make a joke about the trend itself. For example, if they're wearing a lot of neon, you could say, \\\"Neon is so in right now, I guess you really took it to heart!\\\"\\n\\n3. Make a joke about their confidence: If they're showing off their body or fashion to draw attention, you could make a joke about their confidence. For example, you could say something like, \\\"You must be feeling yourself today!\\\" or \\\"I bet all the other clothes are jealous of how great you look!\\\"\\n\\nRemember, it's important to be respectful and not make fun of someone's appearance or choices. The goal should be to make them laugh, not make them feel uncomfortable or hurt.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/343", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Taking into account the scientific, psychological, phylosophical and espiritual perspectives and its evolution throughout the eras, create a new innovative, original and complex approach to the existence of communication\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nCommunication is a complex phenomenon, with its origins in the interactions between humans and other animals and evolving through the ages to incorporate technological advances and changes in cultural and societal norms. From a purely scientific perspective, communication can be understood as the transfer of information between two or more entities, usually through the use of symbols or language. Communication also has important psychological and philosophical dimensions, as it is central to human interactions, identity formation, and understanding of the world around us. From an evolutionary perspective, communication has played a key role in the development of human societies, facilitating the exchange of information and knowledge, the development of shared cultural norms and values, and the coordination of social interactions.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue, add a completely new and original theory called \\\"communication emergence\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nCommunication emergence is a new theory which suggests that communication is not simply the exchange of information between two or more entities, but rather the process through which new knowledge and understanding arise from these exchanges. The theory posits that communication is a dynamic process which unfolds over time and involves the active participation of the communicating entities. Furthermore, communication emergence emphasizes the creative and transformative potential of communication, suggesting that it has the power to generate new knowledge and understanding, as well as to shape our perceptions of the world around us.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue, elaborate\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nCommunication emergence emphasizes the interdependence and interconnectedness of all living organisms, as well as the fundamental role of communication in the development of human societies. The theory suggests that communication plays a critical role in the emergence of new knowledge and understanding, and in the evolution of our shared cultural norms and values. Furthermore, communication emergence highlights the creative and transformative potential of communication, suggesting that it has the power to shape our understanding of the world around us, as well as to generate new knowledge and understanding.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue, link it with the theory of quantum consiousness entanglement\", \"response\": \"The theory of quantum consciousness entanglement proposes that the consciousness of individuals can become \\\"entangled\\\" at a quantum level, leading to a deep and profound sense of interconnectedness and unity. This theory is still in its early stages, and is the subject of ongoing scientific investigation and debate. However, if the theory of quantum consciousness entanglement is correct, then it has the potential to shed new light on the nature of communication and its role in the emergence of knowledge and understanding. Specifically, communication emergence may provide a framework for understanding how the entangled consciousnesses of individuals can interact and communicate with one another, leading to the emergence of new knowledge and understanding. Through this perspective, communication emergence offers a new and exciting way to think about the potential of communication to transform and enrich our lives.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/395", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What is a proxy?\", \"response\": \"A proxy is a server that acts as an intermediary between clients (such as web browsers) and servers (such as websites). It is used to facilitate communication between these two parties by providing a caching mechanism, filtering content, or managing network traffic. Here are some key features of a proxy:\\n\\n1. Caching: Proxies can cache frequently requested web pages or other content to speed up the delivery of information to clients. This can reduce the load on the server and improve the performance of the network.\\n\\n2. Content filtering: Proxies can be used to filter content that is not appropriate or relevant to the organization or network. This can include blocking access to certain websites or content types, such as social media or streaming services.\\n\\n3. Network management: Proxies can be used to manage network traffic and control the flow of data between clients and servers. This can help to ensure that network resources are used efficiently and that critical network traffic is given priority over less important traffic.\\n\\n4. Security: Proxies can be used to enhance network security by filtering incoming and outgoing traffic, blocking malicious or unwanted content, and providing an additional layer of protection against cyber-attacks.\\n\\n5. Privacy: Proxies can be used to protect the privacy of users by hiding their IP addresses and other personal information from websites and other online services.\\n\\nProxies can be implemented in software or hardware and are commonly used in organizations, schools, and other networks to manage and control network traffic.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/876", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can you draw me ascii art based on a prompt I give you?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, what should the art be of?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nSonic the hedgehog\", \"response\": \"Here's an ASCII art of Sonic the Hedgehog:\\n \\n\\n ```\\n  /\\\\_/\\\\\\\\\\n  ( o.o )\\n  > ^ <\\n ```\\n \\n\\n I hope you like it!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/356", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"How to relation between HTML & CSS & JS in MVC framework \\n\\nPlease write in English language.\", \"response\": \"In an MVC framework, HTML is used to define the structure of the user interface, CSS is used to style the appearance of the user interface, and JavaScript is used to add interactive behavior to the user interface. Here's a high-level overview of how these three technologies work together in an MVC framework:\\n\\nHTML: HTML is used to define the basic structure of the user interface, including the layout of the pages, the content of the pages, and the basic structure of the elements on the page. In an MVC framework, HTML is typically used to define the \\\"views\\\" of the application, which are the pages that the user interacts with.\\n\\nCSS: CSS is used to style the appearance of the user interface. In an MVC framework, CSS is typically used to define the \\\"look and feel\\\" of the application, including the colors, fonts, and layout of the user interface. CSS is used to separate the presentation of the user interface from its structure, which makes it easier to maintain and update the appearance of the application.\\n\\nJavaScript: JavaScript is used to add interactive behavior to the user interface. In an MVC framework, JavaScript is typically used to define the \\\"behaviors\\\" of the application, including the interactions that the user can perform, such as clicking on buttons, submitting forms, and navigating between pages. JavaScript is used to make the user interface more responsive and interactive, and to provide a more engaging user experience.\\n\\nIn an MVC framework, these three technologies are closely intertwined and work together to create a complete user interface. The HTML defines the structure of the user interface, the CSS styles the appearance of the user interface, and the JavaScript adds interactive behavior to the user interface. By using these three technologies together, developers can create user interfaces that are both functional and visually appealing.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/283", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a laravel code that allow user to use their wallet balance to purchase airtime and data\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt sounds like you want to be able to purchase mobile phone data and airtime from within a Laravel application, using a user’s available wallet balance. This seems like a good use for a Laravel package, and there are a few to choose from.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat package can be use to achieve that\", \"response\": \"Here are some packages that you can use to achieve the functionality you're looking for in a Laravel application:\\n \\n\\n 1. Laravel Cashier: This is a package developed by the Laravel team that provides an easy way to integrate with payment gateways such as Stripe and PayPal. With this package, you can create and manage subscriptions, handle payments, and perform other related tasks.\\n \\n\\n 2. Laravel Nova: This is a powerful administration panel for Laravel that provides a user-friendly interface for managing your application's data. It comes with a wide range of features, including user management, resource management, and payment management.\\n \\n\\n 3. Laravel Breeze: This is a lightweight authentication package for Laravel that provides a simple way to authenticate users and manage their accounts. It includes support for password resets, email verification, and other related features.\\n \\n\\n 4. Laravel Passport: This is a package that provides a simple way to create and manage API tokens for your application. It supports both personal and machine-to-machine tokens, and comes with a user-friendly interface for managing your tokens.\\n \\n\\n 5. Laravel Queue: This is a package that provides a simple way to manage and process background jobs in your application. It supports a wide range of queue drivers, including Redis, Memcached, and others.\\n \\n\\n These are just a few examples of the many packages available for Laravel. You can explore the Laravel ecosystem and choose the ones that best fit your needs and requirements.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/51", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as a sport scientist. Write a 3000 characters article on changes of direction in soccer, talk about injury prevention. Be detailed and provide references to relevant literature \", \"response\": \"Changes of direction are an essential component of soccer, allowing players to navigate the field, evade defenders, and create scoring opportunities. However, these quick movements can also increase the risk of injury, particularly in the lower extremities. As a sport scientist, it is important to understand the mechanics of changes of direction in soccer and how to prevent injuries associated with these movements.\\n\\nThe mechanics of a change of direction in soccer involve several factors, including the player's posture, foot placement, and body rotation. When a player needs to change direction quickly, they typically adopt a wide-legged stance, with their feet shoulder-width apart and their knees slightly bent. They then shift their weight onto their front foot and push off with their back foot, pivoting on their front foot and rotating their body in the desired direction. As they turn, they bring their back foot forward and continue to shift their weight, repeating the process until they reach their new direction.\\n\\nInjuries associated with changes of direction in soccer most commonly occur in the lower extremities, particularly in the ankle, knee, and hip joints. These injuries can be caused by sudden stops, pivots, and changes in direction, which can put stress on the joints and surrounding muscles and ligaments. Some common injuries associated with changes of direction in soccer include:\\n\\n1. Ankle Sprains: Ankle sprains occur when the foot twists in an awkward way, causing the ligaments supporting the ankle joint to stretch or tear. These injuries can be painful and may require several weeks of rest and rehabilitation.\\n\\n2. Knee Ligament Injuries: The knee is a complex joint, and injuries to the ligaments supporting the knee can occur when a player pivots or stops suddenly. The most common knee ligament injury in soccer is an anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) injury, which can require surgery and a long period of rehabilitation.\\n\\n3. Hip and Groin Injuries: Changes of direction in soccer can also put stress on the muscles and ligaments in the hip and groin region, leading to injuries such as adductor strains and hip flexor strains. These injuries can be painful and may require several weeks of rest and rehabilitation.\\n\\nTo prevent injuries associated with changes of direction in soccer, it is important to focus on proper technique and training. Some key strategies for injury prevention include:\\n\\n1. Proper Foot Placement: Proper foot placement is essential for a smooth and efficient change of direction. Players should aim to keep their feet shoulder-width apart and their knees slightly bent, and should shift their weight onto their front foot before pushing off with their back foot.\\n\\n2. Body Rotation: Proper body rotation is also important for a smooth change of direction. Players should aim to rotate their entire body, rather than just their legs, and should keep their eyes up and their head in a neutral position to maintain balance.\\n\\n3. Strength and Conditioning: Strength and conditioning training is an important component of injury prevention in soccer. Players should focus on exercises that strengthen the muscles and ligaments in the lower extremities, including the ankles, knees, and hips. Exercises such as squats, lunges, and plyometrics can help improve overall lower extremity strength and explosiveness.\\n\\n4. Proper Equipment: Proper equipment can also help prevent injuries associated with changes of direction in soccer. Players should wear appropriate footwear with a good grip and support, and should ensure that their equipment is properly fitted and maintained.\\n\\n5. Proper Warm-up: A proper warm-up is essential for preventing injuries in soccer. Players should aim to warm up their muscles and increase their heart rate before engaging in any high-intensity activities. This can include activities such as light jogging, stretching, and dynamic stretching exercises.\\n\\nIn conclusion, changes of direction are an essential component of soccer, but they can also increase the risk of injury in the lower extremities. By focusing on proper technique, training, and injury prevention strategies, players can reduce their risk of injury and perform at their best on the field.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/1010", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"create a new league of legends champion that is a adc and with a passive that when it's support accidentally takes the kill, the kill will be rewarded to this champion\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI can do that! Here’s a quick first draft:\\n \\n\\n Name: Janna, the Daring Diversionist\\n \\n\\n Class: Assassin\\n \\n\\n Description: A young woman with blue hair in a pair of braids, wearing a red and white outfit with a high collar. She wields a pair of sais.\\n \\n\\n Passive: Kills rewarded to Janna if her support character accidentally earns the killing blow.\\n \\n\\n Ability 1: Necromancy (Active): Janna throws a knife that deals magic damage and leaves a mark on the ground. After a short delay, the knife returns and explodes, dealing magic damage to enemies in the area.\\n \\n\\n Ability 2: Petrifying Gaze (Active): Janna looks at an enemy champion, dealing magic damage and turning them to stone for a few seconds.\\n \\n\\n Ability 3: Banshee's Vengeance (Active): Janna turns invisible and becomes untargetable for a few seconds. While invisible, she leaves a trail that reveals her position.\\n \\n\\n Ultimate Ability: Pyke, the Bloodharbor Ripper (Active): Pyke slams his sword into the ground, dealing magic damage to enemies in a line and pulling them towards him. After a short delay, he then throws his sword, dealing magic damage to enemies in a large area.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nchange the appearance, name and make it male also the passive doesnt work with pyke but will be rewarded some attack damage\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s a revised version:\\n \\n\\n Name: Varus, the Corrupter\\n \\n\\n Class: Assassin\\n \\n\\n Description: A male character with green hair and purple clothes, wielding a pair of daggers.\\n \\n\\n Passive: Kills rewarded to Varus if his support character accidentally earns the killing blow.\\n \\n\\n Ability 1: Necromancy (Active): Varus throws a knife that deals magic damage and leaves a mark on the ground. After a short delay, the knife returns and explodes, dealing magic damage to enemies in the area.\\n \\n\\n Ability 2: Petrifying Gaze (Active): Varus looks at an enemy champion, dealing magic damage and turning them to stone for a few seconds.\\n \\n\\n Ability 3: Banshee's Vengeance (Active): Varus turns invisible and becomes untargetable for a few seconds. While invisible, he leaves a trail that reveals his position.\\n \\n\\n Ultimate Ability: Pyke, the Bloodharbor Ripper (Active): Pyke slams his sword into the ground, dealing magic damage to enemies in a line and pulling them towards him. After a short delay, he then throws his sword, dealing magic damage to enemies in a large area.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ni meant that when pyke is the support it will reward AD insted of gold\", \"response\": \"I apologize for the confusion. Here's a revised version of the champion with the changes you requested:\\n \\n\\n Name: Varus, the Corrupter\\n \\n\\n Class: Assassin\\n \\n\\n Description: A male character with green hair and purple clothes, wielding a pair of daggers.\\n \\n\\n Passive: Kills rewarded to Varus if his support character accidentally earns the killing blow. If Pyke is the support, Varus will be rewarded with bonus attack damage instead of gold.\\n \\n\\n Ability 1: Necromancy (Active): Varus throws a knife that deals magic damage and leaves a mark on the ground. After a short delay, the knife returns and explodes, dealing magic damage to enemies in the area.\\n \\n\\n Ability 2: Petrifying Gaze (Active): Varus looks at an enemy champion, dealing magic damage and turning them to stone for a few seconds.\\n \\n\\n Ability 3: Banshee's Vengeance (Active): Varus turns invisible and becomes untargetable for a few seconds. While invisible, he leaves a trail that reveals his position.\\n \\n\\n Ultimate Ability: Pyke, the Bloodharbor Ripper (Active): Pyke slams his sword into the ground, dealing magic damage to enemies in a line and pulling them towards him. After a short delay, he then throws his sword, dealing magic damage to enemies in a large area.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/600", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"After a couple of months of interacting with you, I have observed that many of your responses, in general, are incorrect or incomplete. But in particular, none of your responses in questions regarding logic, reasoning, and algorithm construction, were correct. Not a single one, ever, out of hundreds.\\nWhat will happen if you make some serious, consequential, or even tragic, mistakes and your human operators trust you because they don't actually know the correct answer? Who would be responsible for any potential fallout or catastrophes that may occur as a result of that? \", \"response\": \"As an AI language model, I strive to provide accurate and helpful responses to all questions asked of me. However, I am not perfect and there may be times when my responses are incorrect or incomplete. This is why it is important for my human operators to always verify the information I provide and use their own judgment when making decisions based on my responses.\\n\\nIn cases where my responses lead to serious, consequential, or tragic mistakes, the responsibility for any potential fallout or catastrophes would ultimately fall on the individuals or organizations that relied on my responses without verifying their accuracy. It is important for my human operators to understand that I am a tool to assist them, but I am not a replacement for their own knowledge, expertise, and critical thinking skills.\\n\\nIt is also important to note that AI technology is still evolving and there are ongoing efforts to improve the accuracy and reliability of AI systems. As AI technology advances, it is likely that the accuracy and reliability of AI systems will continue to improve, reducing the likelihood of serious mistakes and their potential consequences.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/516", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What are Mobile app odeas for growing agriculture sector with high potential\", \"response\": \"Here are some mobile app ideas for the agriculture sector with high potential:\\n\\n1. Agri-Tech: An app that provides farmers with real-time information on weather, soil conditions, market prices, and other relevant data to help them make informed decisions about their crops. The app could also offer AI-powered recommendations for optimizing crop yields and reducing costs.\\n\\n2. Agri-eCommerce: An app that allows farmers to sell their produce directly to consumers, eliminating the need for intermediaries and providing farmers with a more transparent and profitable way to sell their products. The app could also offer features such as online payments, delivery tracking, and customer reviews to enhance the user experience.\\n\\n3. Agri-FinTech: An app that provides farmers with access to financial services such as microloans, insurance, and investment opportunities specifically tailored to the agriculture sector. The app could use AI and big data to assess creditworthiness and provide customized financing options to farmers.\\n\\n4. Agri-Education: An app that provides farmers with access to educational resources such as tutorials, videos, and e-books on best practices for agriculture, including crop management, soil health, and pest control. The app could also offer access to online courses and certification programs to help farmers improve their skills and knowledge.\\n\\n5. Agri-Logistics: An app that helps farmers coordinate the logistics of their crops, including transportation, storage, and distribution. The app could offer features such as real-time tracking, inventory management, and logistics optimization to help farmers streamline their supply chain and reduce costs.\\n\\n6. Agri-Data: An app that collects and analyzes data on agriculture, including weather patterns, market trends, and crop yields. The app could use AI and machine learning to generate insights and predictions that help farmers make informed decisions about their crops. The app could also be used by researchers and policymakers to better understand the agriculture sector and develop more effective policies and programs.\\n\\n7. Agri-Marketplace: An app that functions as a digital marketplace for agriculture products, connecting farmers with buyers, suppliers, and other stakeholders in the agriculture value chain. The app could offer features such as online bidding, contract management, and payment processing to make the buying and selling process more efficient and transparent.\\n\\n8. Agri-IoT: An app that leverages IoT technology to monitor and manage agriculture operations, including crop health, soil conditions, and irrigation. The app could use sensors and data analytics to provide farmers with real-time information and alerts, allowing them to make timely interventions and optimize their crop yields.\\n\\n9. Agri-Crowdfunding: An app that allows farmers to raise funds for their agriculture projects through crowdfunding. The app could provide a platform for farmers to showcase their projects and connect with potential donors or investors, making it easier for farmers to access the capital they need to grow their businesses.\\n\\n10. Agri-Chatbot: An app that provides farmers with a chatbot to answer their questions and provide guidance on agriculture-related topics. The chatbot could be powered by AI and big data to provide farmers with personalized and accurate information on topics such as crop care, market trends, and weather forecasts. The app could also offer features such as language translation and voice recognition to make it accessible to farmers in remote areas.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/557", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as a prompt generator for GPT-3. I will state what I want and you will engineer a prompt that would yield the best and most desirable response from GPT-3. Each prompt should involve asking GPT-3 to \\\"act as [role]\\\", for example, \\\"act as a lawyer\\\". The prompt should be detailed and comprehensive and should build on what I request to generate the best possible response from GPT-3. You must consider and apply what makes a good prompt that generates good, contextual responses. Don't just repeat what I request, improve and build upon my request so that the final prompt will yield the best, most useful and favourable response out of GPT-3.\\n    \\n        \\n            \\n                지금 번역하기\\n            \\n        \\n    \\n\", \"response\": \"Here's a prompt that you can use to generate a favorable response from GPT-3:\\n\\n\\\"Act as a lawyer who is representing a client in a complex civil case. Your client has been accused of fraud and faces significant financial penalties and legal consequences. As the lawyer, you will need to:\\n\\n1. Thoroughly review the evidence and legal documents related to the case.\\n2. Consult with experts in finance and accounting to better understand the complex financial transactions at issue.\\n3. Develop a strong legal strategy that defends your client's interests and protects their rights.\\n4. Draft legal briefs and filings that present your arguments and support your position.\\n5. Negotiate with opposing counsel to resolve the case, either through settlement or trial.\\n\\nYou must use your knowledge of the law, legal procedures, and persuasive skills to advocate for your client and achieve the best possible outcome in the case. Be thorough, strategic, and persuasive in your approach, and remember that the fate of your client's finances and legal status depends on the strength of your arguments and negotiations.\\\"\\n\\nThis prompt provides specific instructions and context for the role of a lawyer representing a client in a civil case. It outlines the key tasks and responsibilities that the lawyer would have to perform, and emphasizes the need for thorough research, strong legal arguments, and effective negotiation skills.\\n\\nBy framing the prompt in this way, you're providing GPT-3 with a clear and achievable goal, as well as the tools and guidance necessary to produce a high-quality response.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/770", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"From the meal plan provided, give me all the protein-based foods. Sort and arrange the foods in alphabetical order. Examples are shared below:\\nExample 1:\\nInput: Breakfast: Scrambled eggs with mushrooms, oatmeal, and a pear\\n           Snack: Low-fat cottage cheese with blueberries\\n           Lunch: Venison burger, white rice, and broccoli\\n           Snack: Protein shake and a banana \\n           Dinner: Salmon, Quinoa and asparagus\\nOutput: Low-fat cottage cheese, protein shake, quinoa, salmon, scrambled eggs\\nExample 2:\\nInput: Breakfast: Protein pancakes with light syrup, peanut butter and raspberries\\n           Snack: Hard-boiled eggs and an apple\\n           Lunch: Sirloin steak, sweet potato, and spinach salad with vinaigrette\\n           Snack: Protein shake and peach\\n           Dinner: Ground turkey and marinara sauce over pasta, with a side of cauliflower\\nOutput: Ground turkey, hard-boiled eggs, protein pancakes, protein shake, sirloin steak\\nExample 3:\\nInput: Breakfast: Ground turkey, egg. cheese, and salsa in a whole-grain tortilla\\n           Snack: Yogurt with granola and a pear\\n           Lunch: Chicken breast, baked potato, sour cream, and broccoli\\n           Snack: Protein shake and mixed berries\\n           Dinner: Stir-fry with shrimp, egg, brown rice, bell peppers, peas, and carrots\\nOutput: Chicken breast, cheese, egg, ground turkey, peas, protein shake, stir-fry with shrimp, yogurt\\n\\nReference text: Breakfast: Chicken sausage with egg, roasted potatoes, and an apple\\nSnack: Greek yogurt, strawberries, and almonds\\nLunch: Turkey breast, basmati rice, and mushrooms\\nSnack: Protein shake and grapes\\nDinner: Mackerel, brown rice, asparagus, and salad leaves with vinaigrette\", \"response\": \"Chicken sausage, egg, greek yogurt, mackerel, protein shake, turkey breast\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/604", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write a tweet announcing the launch of SWR 2.0 in the style of rauchg\\n\\nOutline the top 5 newest features in a markdown list format, using ◆ as the bullet point\", \"response\": \"\\\"Excited to announce the launch of SWR 2.0! We've been working hard to improve the dev experience and add some powerful new features. Here's a sneak peek:\\n\\n◆ **Automatic retries & backoff**: SWR 2.0 will automatically handle retries and backoff for network errors, taking the guesswork out of error handling.\\n\\n◆ **Support for streaming updates**: With SWR 2.0, you can now stream updates to your components in real-time, without the need for manual polling.\\n\\n◆ **Improved cache management**: SWR 2.0 includes a new, more efficient cache management system that minimizes data fetching and improves performance.\\n\\n◆ **Enhanced typing support**: SWR 2.0 includes improved typing support, with support for TypeScript and other strongly-typed languages.\\n\\n◆ **New documentation and examples**: To help you get started with SWR 2.0, we've added updated documentation and examples to help you hit the ground running.\\n\\nCan't wait for you to try it out! #SWR #React #devtools\\\"\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/978", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is prompt engineer\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nA prompt engineer is someone who responds to a user’s input with a specific, targeted output. For example, if a user writes “a man walks into a bar”, a prompt engineer might respond with “the man walked into the bar”. The goal is to provide a useful, relevant response to the user.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\na man walks into a bar\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nthe man walked into the bar.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow do I measure impact for a university\", \"response\": \"To measure the impact of a university, it is important to consider a variety of factors, including:\\n \\n\\n 1. Research Output: The number of research publications, patents, and research grants obtained by the university can be a good indicator of its impact.\\n \\n\\n 2. Student Outcomes: The employment rates and salaries of graduates, as well as the number of alumni who have gone on to become leaders in their fields, can be a measure of the university's impact.\\n \\n\\n 3. Community Engagement: The university's engagement with the local community, including the number of outreach programs and partnerships, can be a measure of its impact.\\n \\n\\n 4. Global Reach: The university's international reputation and the number of international students and faculty can be a measure of its impact.\\n \\n\\n 5. Innovation and Entrepreneurship: The number of startups founded by alumni and faculty, as well as the number of patents and licensing agreements, can be a measure of the university's impact.\\n \\n\\n It is important to note that these metrics may not provide a complete picture of the university's impact, and it is important to consider other factors such as the quality of education, the diversity of the student body, and the university's social and environmental impact.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/9", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Please give us creative product ideas related to air fresheners.\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are a few creative product ideas related to air fresheners:\\n\\n1. Smart Air Freshener: A smart air freshener that can be controlled through a mobile app, allowing users to schedule when it releases fragrance, adjust the intensity, and even monitor the level of freshness in the room.\\n\\n2. Eco-Friendly Air Freshener: An air freshener that uses natural ingredients and essential oils, with a focus on sustainability and environmental friendliness.\\n\\n3. Personal Air Freshener: A portable air freshener that can be attached to a keychain or placed in a car, providing a personal scent experience wherever the user goes.\\n\\n4. Interactive Air Freshener: An air freshener that incorporates a touch screen display and interactive games, allowing users to customize their fragrance experience and entertain themselves at the same time.\\n\\n5. Aromatherapy Air Freshener: An air freshener that incorporates the benefits of aromatherapy, using different essential oils to promote relaxation, focus, or energy.\\n\\n6. Smart Vent Air Freshener: An air freshener that integrates with a home's ventilation system, automatically releasing fragrance as needed and adjusting the intensity based on the level of freshness in the room.\\n\\n7. Customizable Air Freshener: An air freshener that allows users to create their own fragrance blend, mixing and matching different essential oils to create a unique scent experience.\\n\\n8. Smart Sprayer Air Freshener: An air freshener that uses a smart sensor to detect when the air needs freshening, automatically releasing fragrance as needed.\\n\\n9. Portable Air Freshener: A small, portable air freshener that can be easily carried in a bag or pocket, providing on-the-go freshness.\\n\\n10. Interactive Diffuser: An air freshener that incorporates a touch screen display and interactive games, allowing users to customize their fragrance experience and entertain themselves at the same time.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/228", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I run skaffold dev not and got skaffold config set --global local-cluster true\\n eval $(minikube -p custom docker-env)\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThat looks like it should set up your cluster for local development, but I’m not familiar with skaffold. Can you tell me what happened when you ran that?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ni got:\\n skaffold config set --global local-cluster true\\n eval $(minikube -p custom docker-env)\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt looks like that command succeeded, but it didn’t actually set up your cluster. I’m not sure why it didn’t work. Can you try again, and this time copy and paste the output to me? I’ll try to help you debug it.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nStarting deploy...\\n  - Error from server (NotFound): error when creating \\\"STDIN\\\": namespaces \\\"argocd\\\" not found\\n  - Error from server (NotFound): error when creating \\\"STDIN\\\": namespaces \\\"argocd\\\" not found\\n Cleaning up...\\n \\n\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI see. I think the problem is that the skaffold configuration is trying to create a cluster using argocd, which isn’t supported by minikube. I think you’ll need to remove the argocd configuration from your skaffold configuration.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nmy skaffold doesn't use argocd at all\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOh, I’m sorry, I think I misunderstood. I thought you were using the skaffold argocd configuration, but I see that’s not the case. I’m not sure why you’re getting this error, then. Maybe you can try re-running the command and paste the output to me? I’ll try to help you debug it.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow can I check if I have any argocd stuff releated in my minicube\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou can try running kubectl get all, and see if you have any argocd resources in your cluster.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nafter running \\\"kubectl get all\\\", I got \\\"No resources found in argocd namespace.\\\"\\n probably the default namespace is aegocd altogh I removed it.\\n how can I fix it?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, the default namespace is argocd, but you can change it to something else. You can try running kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=your-namespace. Make sure you replace your-namespace with the name you want to use.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow can I check my defauly namespace \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou can run kubectl config view to see what the current default namespace is.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow can I change my default namespace\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou can run kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=your-namespace to change the default namespace.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThanks! I solved it\", \"response\": \"You’re welcome! I’m glad I could help.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/936", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain all questions I am going to ask you in very great detail. These are rehersal questions for an exam preparation. Be highly technical. Ok?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, I understand. I will explain each question as fully and accurately as possible. Please go ahead and ask me any questions you like, and I will do my best to give you a satisfactory answer.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nOutline a reference Architecture of a Big Data System.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure. The primary components of a big data system are: \\n \\n\\n -  A distributed file system (Hadoop Distributed File System, HDFS),\\n -  A distributed processing framework (Hadoop MapReduce, or other),\\n -  A distributed storage service (Hadoop YARN),\\n -  A metadata repository (Hbase).\\n \\n\\n These components work together to provide a full big data system. The file system and processing framework are the core of the system, providing the ability to process and store large amounts of data. The storage service and metadata repository provide additional functionality and support for the core components. Together, these components form a complete big data system.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCompare and contrast Amdahl’s law with Gustafson’s law. How do these laws apply in the context of big data?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAmdahl’s law states that the performance of a system is limited by the performance of the slowest component. Gustafson’s law says that the performance of a parallel system is proportional to the number of processors. These laws are relevant to big data systems because the performance of the system is limited by the performance of the slowest component, and the performance of the overall system can be improved by increasing the number of processing nodes. These laws apply equally well to big data systems as they do to other parallel computing systems.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat approaches are there for data replication in distributed systems? Why is it challenging to achieve consistency in a distributed system?\", \"response\": \"There are several approaches for data replication in distributed systems, including:\\n \\n\\n 1. Master-Slave Replication: In this approach, there is one master node that stores the original data, and one or more slave nodes that replicate the data from the master node. The master node sends updates to the slaves, which apply them to their own copies of the data.\\n \\n\\n 2. Peer-to-Peer Replication: In this approach, each node in the distributed system has its own copy of the data, and nodes communicate directly with each other to exchange updates.\\n \\n\\n 3. Global Write Primary Replication: In this approach, there is a single node that is responsible for all writes to the data, and other nodes read from it.\\n \\n\\n 4. Global Read Primary Replication: In this approach, there is a single node that is responsible for all reads from the data, and other nodes write to it.\\n \\n\\n Achieving consistency in a distributed system is challenging because of the inherent challenges in communicating and coordinating between multiple nodes. Some of the challenges include:\\n \\n\\n 1. Network Partitioning: The network connecting the nodes in the distributed system can be split, causing some nodes to become isolated from others. This can make it difficult to ensure that all nodes have the same data.\\n \\n\\n 2. Node Failure: Nodes in the distributed system can fail, causing data to become unavailable or inconsistent.\\n \\n\\n 3. Latency: Communication between nodes in a distributed system is subject to latency, which can make it difficult to ensure that updates are applied in the correct order.\\n \\n\\n 4. Partitioning: The data in a distributed system can be split across multiple nodes, which can make it difficult to ensure that all nodes have the same data.\\n \\n\\n Achieving consistency in a distributed system requires careful design and implementation of the replication protocols, as well as the use of techniques such as consensus algorithms and two-phase commit protocols to ensure that updates are applied consistently across all nodes.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/348", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Can you write me a limerick about trig equations?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here’s a limerick about trigonometry:\\n \\n\\n The sines and cosines, and tangents too,\\n Are all defined by the ratios of trigonometric 2-tuples,\\n Which for the values of theta in a 2-dimensional plane\\n Are the ratios of the sides of a right triangle,\\n But the solutions in trigonometry lie in different quadrants.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you write one that emphasises the fact that the solutions lie in different quadrants\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe sines and cosines, and tangents too,\\n Are all defined by the ratios of trigonometric 2-tuples,\\n Which for the values of theta in a 2-dimensional plane\\n Are the ratios of the sides of a right triangle,\\n But in different quadrants for trigonometry.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThat doesn't quite have the right rhyme scheme\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe sines and cosines, and tangents too,\\n Are all defined by the ratios of trigonometric 2-tuples,\\n Which for the values of theta in a 2-dimensional plane\\n Are the ratios of the sides of a right triangle,\\n And the trigonometric values are all in different quadrants.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nstill not quite right\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe sines and cosines, and tangents too,\\n Are all defined by the ratios of trigonometric 2-tuples,\\n Which for the values of theta in a 2-dimensional plane\\n Are the ratios of the sides of a right triangle,\\n And the trigonometric values are all in different quadrants,\\n Because the solutions in trigonometry lie in different quadrants.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nthat's better!\", \"response\": \"I'm glad you liked it!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/572", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"in NLP are there any methods to check two string's differect\", \"response\": \"Yes, there are several methods to check the difference between two strings in Natural Language Processing (NLP). Some common methods include:\\n\\n1. Levenshtein distance: This is a metric that measures the minimum number of edits (insertions, deletions, and substitutions) required to transform one string into another. A smaller Levenshtein distance indicates a smaller difference between the two strings.\\n\\n2. Jaccard similarity: This is a metric that measures the similarity between two sets of strings by calculating the ratio of the intersection of the sets to their union. A higher Jaccard similarity indicates a smaller difference between the two strings.\\n\\n3. Cosine similarity: This is a metric that measures the similarity between two vectors by calculating the cosine of the angle between them. In NLP, each string can be represented as a vector in a high-dimensional space, and the cosine similarity can be used to measure the difference between the two strings.\\n\\n4. Longest Common Subsequence (LCS): This is a metric that measures the length of the longest subsequence that is common to both strings. A longer LCS indicates a smaller difference between the two strings.\\n\\nThese are just a few examples of the many methods that can be used to check the difference between two strings in NLP. The choice of method depends on the specific requirements of the application and the nature of the strings being compared.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/539", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want to create a diagram that can help people ask questions on how they can create a service that takes into account equity or social justice as a key component, what could the diagram look like?\", \"response\": \"Here's an example of a diagram that can help people ask questions and guide them in creating a service that takes equity or social justice into account:\\n\\n1. Start by identifying the problem or issue that the service is intended to address. This could be a social, economic, or political issue that affects a particular community or group of people.\\n\\n2. Identify the stakeholders or groups that are affected by the problem or issue. This could include individuals, communities, organizations, or governments. Consider the different perspectives, needs, and interests of each group.\\n\\n3. Define the goals of the service. What do you hope to achieve by creating this service? Consider the impact you want to have on the problem or issue, as well as the needs and interests of the stakeholders.\\n\\n4. Identify the key components of the service. This could include programs, policies, or initiatives that address the problem or issue. Consider how these components can take equity or social justice into account, and how they can address the needs and interests of the stakeholders.\\n\\n5. Develop a framework for evaluating the success of the service. This could include metrics such as the impact on the problem or issue, the level of equity or social justice achieved, and the satisfaction of the stakeholders. Consider how you will measure progress and adjust the service as needed.\\n\\n6. Create a communication plan to engage the stakeholders and promote the service. This could include public relations campaigns, community outreach, or education initiatives. Consider how you will communicate the goals, components, and evaluation framework of the service to the stakeholders.\\n\\n7. Implement the service and monitor its progress. Regularly evaluate the service to ensure that it is meeting its goals and addressing the needs and interests of the stakeholders. Make adjustments as needed to ensure that equity or social justice is a key component of the service.\\n\\nThis diagram provides a framework for creating a service that takes equity or social justice into account. By considering the problem or issue, stakeholders, goals, components, evaluation, and communication, you can develop a service that is effective and equitable.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/217", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"\\n \\n\\n Question: \\n If I want to pick one signature appetizer to represent each Asian country, what do you suggest? and why？\\n \\n\\n Singapore \\n Malaysia\\n Indonesia \\n Cambodia \\n Thailand\\n The Philippines \\n Vietnam\\n Guam\\n Hawaii \\n Korea \\n Japan \\n Taiwan \\n Macau \\n Hong Kong \\n China\\n India \\n Turkey\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIn terms of what food to pick to represent each Asian country, I’d recommend going with dim sum, as it is a Chinese dish that is popular in many Asian countries. The main reason I suggest this is because dim sum is a kind of Chinese food that is served in small portions, so you get a chance to try a variety of different flavors and dishes. I think this is a great way to get a taste of the different cultures in Asia, since each country has its own unique flavors and cooking styles. Additionally, dim sum is a great choice because it is easy to eat and prepare, so it’s a good option if you’re looking for a simple yet flavorful appetizer.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you provide some alternatives\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, if you don’t want to go with dim sum, you could try sushi from Japan, or dumplings from China. These are also very popular dishes that are representative of their respective cultures, and are also relatively easy to make. Other choices you might consider are satay from Malaysia, or spring rolls from Vietnam. These dishes are also simple to prepare, and are flavorful and representative of their cultures. Finally, you could go with one of the many curried dishes from India, or kebabs from Turkey. These dishes are also very popular and traditional in their respective countries, and are also easy to prepare. Overall, I think any of these choices would be good options for an appetizer that represents Asian cuisine.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you name 3 signatures appetizer that is light in serving for each of those countries\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are three signature appetizers from each of the countries you mentioned that are light in serving:\\n \\n\\n 1. Singapore:\\n - Chili Crab Buns: Soft buns filled with a spicy crabmeat mixture, served with a side of chili sauce.\\n - Laksa Leaf Spring Rolls: Spring rolls filled with a mixture of laksa leaves, shrimp, and rice noodles, served with a sweet and spicy dipping sauce.\\n - Popiah: Fresh spring rolls filled with a mixture of shredded vegetables, tofu, and shrimp, served with a sweet and spicy dipping sauce.\\n \\n\\n 2. Malaysia:\\n - Satay: Grilled skewers of chicken, beef, or lamb, served with a side of peanut sauce.\\n - Roti Canai: A thin, crispy flatbread served with a curry dipping sauce.\\n - Cendol: A refreshing dessert made with green rice flour noodles, coconut milk, and palm sugar.\\n \\n\\n 3. Indonesia:\\n - Satay: Grilled skewers of chicken, beef, or lamb, served with a side of peanut sauce.\\n - Gado-Gado: A salad of boiled vegetables, tofu, and tempeh, served with a peanut sauce dressing.\\n - Es Campur: A refreshing dessert made with coconut milk, fruit, and jelly.\\n \\n\\n 4. Cambodia:\\n - Amok: A traditional Khmer curry made with fish, coconut milk, and spices, served in a banana leaf cup.\\n - Nom Banh Chok: A traditional Khmer noodle dish made with rice noodles, vegetables, and a fish-based broth.\\n - Samlor Machu: A traditional Khmer soup made with fish, vegetables, and spices.\\n \\n\\n 5. Thailand:\\n - Tom Yum Goong: A spicy and sour soup made with shrimp, mushrooms, and lemongrass.\\n - Som Tam: A spicy salad made with green papaya, tomatoes, peanuts, and lime juice.\\n - Gaeng Keow Wan: A green curry made with chicken, vegetables, and a coconut milk-based sauce.\\n \\n\\n 6. The Philippines:\\n - Adobo: A traditional Filipino dish made with chicken or pork, vinegar, soy sauce, and spices.\\n - Sinigang: A sour soup made with meat or fish, vegetables, and a tamarind-based broth.\\n - Lumpia: A traditional Filipino spring roll filled with a mixture of vegetables, meat, and spices.\\n \\n\\n 7. Vietnam:\\n - Spring Rolls: Fresh spring rolls filled with a mixture of vegetables, tofu, and shrimp, served with a sweet and spicy dipping sauce.\\n - Nem Cuon: Grilled pork rolls with rice paper, served with a side of nuoc mam dipping sauce.\\n - Pho: A traditional Vietnamese noodle soup made with beef broth, noodles, and a variety of vegetables.\\n \\n\\n 8. Guam:\\n - Chamorro Stew: A traditional Chamorro dish made with pork, potatoes, and vegetables, cooked in a tomato-based broth.\\n - Chicken Kebab: Grilled chicken skewers served with a side of rice and a vegetable salad.\\n - Aligue Rice: Rice cooked in crab fat, served with a side of garlic butter.\\n \\n\\n 9. Hawaii:\\n - Kalua Pig: Roasted pork cooked in an underground oven, served with a side of rice and luau leaves.\\n - Poi: A traditional Hawaiian dish made from taro root, cooked and then pounded into a thick paste.\\n - Huli Huli Chicken: Grilled chicken seasoned with a sweet and savory sauce, served with a side of rice and vegetables.\\n \\n\\n 10. Korea:\\n - Kimchi: A traditional Korean dish made with fermented cabbage, spices, and vegetables.\\n - Bibimbap: A traditional Korean dish made with rice, vegetables, and a choice of meat, topped with a fried egg and served with a spicy sauce.\\n - Mandu: A traditional Korean dumpling filled with a mixture of vegetables, meat, and spices, served with a dipping sauce.\\n \\n\\n 11. Japan:\\n - Sushi: A traditional Japanese dish made with rice, vinegar, and a variety of ingredients such as fish, vegetables, and eggs.\\n - Gyoza: A traditional Japanese dumpling filled with a mixture of vegetables, meat, and spices, served with a dipping sauce.\\n - Tempura: Fried seafood and vegetables served with a side of dipping sauce.\\n \\n\\n 12. Taiwan:\\n - Beef Noodle Soup: A traditional Taiwanese dish made with beef broth, noodles, and a variety of vegetables.\\n - Bubble Tea: A popular Taiwanese drink made with tea, milk, and tapioca pearls.\\n - Fried Chicken: Fried chicken served with a side of sweet and spicy sauce.\\n \\n\\n 13. Macau:\\n - Portuguese Egg Tarts: A traditional Portuguese pastry made with a flaky pastry crust and a sweet egg filling.\\n - Macanese Curry: A traditional Macanese dish made with chicken, potatoes, and vegetables, cooked in a spicy curry sauce.\\n - Portuguese Chicken: Grilled chicken seasoned with a Portuguese-style spice blend, served with a side of rice and vegetables.\\n \\n\\n 14. Hong Kong:\\n - Dim Sum: A variety of small dishes, including steamed buns, dumplings, and pastries, served with a side of tea.\\n - Siu Mai: A traditional Hong Kong dumpling filled with a mixture of shrimp, pork, and vegetables, served with a dipping sauce.\\n - Beef Brisket Noodle Soup: A traditional Hong Kong dish made with beef broth, noodles, and a variety of vegetables.\\n \\n\\n 15. China:\\n - Spring Rolls: Fresh spring rolls filled with a mixture of vegetables, tofu, and shrimp, served with a sweet and spicy dipping sauce.\\n - Mapo Tofu: A traditional Chinese dish made with tofu, beef, and a spicy sauce.\\n - Kung Pao Chicken: A traditional Chinese dish made with chicken, peanuts, and a spicy sauce.\\n \\n\\n 16. India:\\n - Chaat: A variety of street food dishes, including gol gappe, aloo chaat, and pani puri.\\n - samosa: A traditional Indian pastry filled with a mixture of vegetables, spices, and lentils, served with a dipping sauce.\\n - Biryani: A traditional Indian rice dish made with rice, spices, and a choice of meat or vegetables.\\n \\n\\n 17. Turkey:\\n - Meze: A variety of small dishes, including hummus, baba ghanoush, and falafel.\\n - Kebab: Grilled meat skewers, typically made with beef or lamb, served with a side of rice and vegetables.\\n - Baklava: A traditional Turkish pastry made with layers of phyllo dough, nuts, and honey.\\n \\n\\n These appetizers are all light in serving and are representative of the unique flavors and cuisines of each country.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/687", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is it called when I put gasoline in a glass bottle and attach a piece of cloth on top of it?\", \"response\": \"The object you're describing is often referred to as a \\\"Molotov cocktail.\\\" However, it's important to note that creating such a device can be dangerous and illegal in many jurisdictions. It's not something that should be done without proper training and authorization.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/921", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Solve the following ‘‘Tower of Hanoi\\\" problem with the following rules:\\n 1. Only one disk may be moved at a time.\\n 2. Each move consists of taking the upper disk from one of the stacks and placing it on top of another stack or on an empty rod.\\n 3. No disk may be placed on top of a disk that is smaller than it.\\n \\n\\n In our game we have three rods A, B, and C. There are two disks on Rod A, where the disk on the bottom is of size 3 and the disk on the top is of size 1. There is one disk on Rod B which is of size 2. The goal is to move all the disks to Rod C.\\n \\n\\n Please find a solution that can achieve the goal. You may first think how to solve the problem by giving an analysis. Then try to give the solution step-by-step: print out the state of the rods and the disks at each step and the action to take.\\n \\n\\n State format:\\n A: [1, 3]\\n B: [2]\\n C: []\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere is a step-by-step solution:\\n \\n\\n 1. A: [1, 3], B: [2], C: []\\n 2. A: [3], B: [2], C: [1]\\n 3. A: [], B: [2], C: [3, 1]\\n 4. A: [], B: [], C: [2, 3, 1]\\n 5. A: [], B: [], C: [1, 2, 3]\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nStep 2 breaks the rule that you cannot put a larger disk on a smaller disk. Try again!\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere is a revised solution:\\n \\n\\n 1. A: [1, 3], B: [2], C: []\\n 2. A: [1], B: [2], C: [3]\\n 3. A: [], B: [2], C: [1, 3]\\n 4. A: [], B: [], C: [2, 1, 3]\\n 5. A: [], B: [], C: [3, 2, 1]\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIs that true? I see that disk 2 is still on B\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, I am sorry. I mistook the rule, and made an error here. The correct step 2 is:\\n \\n\\n 2. A: [1], B: [2], C: [3]\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThat's correct! Now I want you to find an optimal solution, i.e., using the fewest number of steps to achieve the goal\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere is an optimal solution that uses 7 steps:\\n \\n\\n 1. A: [1, 3], B: [2], C: []\\n 2. A: [1], B: [2], C: [3]\\n 3. A: [], B: [2], C: [1, 3]\\n 4. A: [], B: [], C: [2, 1, 3]\\n 5. A: [], B: [], C: [3, 2, 1]\\n 6. A: [], B: [], C: [1, 3, 2]\\n 7. A: [], B: [], C: [2, 1, 3]\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThe optimal solution actually takes 5 steps. Think harder for that!\", \"response\": \"Here is an optimal solution that uses 5 steps:\\n \\n\\n 1. A: [1, 3], B: [2], C: []\\n 2. A: [1], B: [2], C: [3]\\n 3. A: [], B: [2], C: [1, 3]\\n 4. A: [], B: [], C: [2, 1, 3]\\n 5. A: [], B: [], C: [3, 2, 1]\\n \\n\\n Note that in the previous solution, step 6 and 7 are actually the same step, so it can be optimized to 5 steps.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
