{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/177", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"using angular and or javascript what is the best way to use A PC's voice to text built in services to take a converations two users are having with webrtc and convert that audio to text\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think the best way to do that would be to use a combination of angular, webrtc, and the Google Web Speech API. The Google Web Speech API provides a JavaScript interface to the speech recognition capabilities of the user’s speech-enabled device. So you could use that API to listen to the user’s speech, and then use angular to convert the recognized speech to text. You could also use angular to send the recognized text to the other user via webrtc.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwould the above solution work on mobile device \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, that should work on a mobile device. The Google Web Speech API provides a cross-platform speech recognition capability. So you could use it to listen to the user’s speech on any device that has speech recognition capabilities.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow would i take the above solution and do realtime language translation\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou could use a combination of angular, webrtc, and the Google Translate API. The Google Translate API provides a JavaScript interface to the real-time translation capabilities of Google Translate. So you could use the Translate API to translate the user’s speech into another language, and then use angular to convert the translated speech to text. You could also use angular to send the translated text to the other user via webrtc.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nusing the above, can one devices transcribe both sides of the conversation both inbound and outbound\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, you could use the Google Web Speech API on one device to listen to the speech of both users, and then use angular to convert the speech to text on both devices. You could also use angular to send the recognized text to both users via webrtc.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan we add to option to identify which device is best suited to handle the transcription based on connection strength and device\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, you could use the WebRTC API to determine the connection strength between the two devices, and then use that information to determine which device is best suited to handle the transcription.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan we add the option to write to a local file, indicating which source of audio and timing stamping \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, you could use the WebRTC API to write the audio from both devices to a local file. You could also use angular to time-stamp the audio and indicate which source it came from.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwe would then want to post this file to GPT and ask for a summary of the conversation, with each audio sources identified as a speaker.  What is the best way to do that and what are the option\", \"response\": \"You could use the GPT API to summarize the audio file. You could also use angular to identify the audio sources as speakers. You could do this by using the WebRTC API to write the audio from both devices to a local file, and then using angular to time-stamp the audio and indicate which source it came from. You could then use the GPT API to summarize the audio file, and use angular to identify the audio sources as speakers.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/937", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain all questions I am going to ask you in very great detail. These are rehersal questions for an exam preparation. Be highly technical. Ok?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, I understand. I will explain each question as fully and accurately as possible. Please go ahead and ask me any questions you like, and I will do my best to give you a satisfactory answer.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nOutline a reference Architecture of a Big Data System.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure. The primary components of a big data system are: \\n \\n\\n -  A distributed file system (Hadoop Distributed File System, HDFS),\\n -  A distributed processing framework (Hadoop MapReduce, or other),\\n -  A distributed storage service (Hadoop YARN),\\n -  A metadata repository (Hbase).\\n \\n\\n These components work together to provide a full big data system. The file system and processing framework are the core of the system, providing the ability to process and store large amounts of data. The storage service and metadata repository provide additional functionality and support for the core components. Together, these components form a complete big data system.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCompare and contrast Amdahl’s law with Gustafson’s law. How do these laws apply in the context of big data?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAmdahl’s law states that the performance of a system is limited by the performance of the slowest component. Gustafson’s law says that the performance of a parallel system is proportional to the number of processors. These laws are relevant to big data systems because the performance of the system is limited by the performance of the slowest component, and the performance of the overall system can be improved by increasing the number of processing nodes. These laws apply equally well to big data systems as they do to other parallel computing systems.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat approaches are there for data replication in distributed systems? Why is it challenging to achieve consistency in a distributed system?\", \"response\": \"There are several approaches for data replication in distributed systems, including:\\n \\n\\n 1. Master-slave replication: In this approach, a master node replicates its data to one or more slave nodes. The master node is responsible for updating the data, and the slave nodes periodically check for updates and replicate the data to their own local storage. This approach is simple and efficient, but it can be vulnerable to data loss if the master node fails or becomes unresponsive.\\n \\n\\n 2. Peer-to-peer replication: In this approach, each node in the distributed system is responsible for replicating its own data to other nodes in the system. This approach eliminates the need for a master node, and it can be more resilient to failures than the master-slave approach. However, it can be more complex to implement and can require more resources, as each node must perform both read and write operations.\\n \\n\\n 3. Asynchronous replication: In this approach, nodes in the distributed system replicate data to each other in a asynchronous manner. This means that nodes do not wait for a response from the other node before continuing with their own operations. Asynchronous replication can be more efficient than synchronous replication, as it does not require nodes to wait for a response from other nodes before continuing with their own operations. However, it can be more challenging to ensure consistency in the system, as there may be a delay between the time when data is updated on one node and when it is replicated to other nodes.\\n \\n\\n 4. Synchronous replication: In this approach, nodes in the distributed system replicate data to each other in a synchronous manner. This means that nodes wait for a response from the other node before continuing with their own operations. Synchronous replication can provide greater consistency and reliability, as it ensures that all nodes in the system have the most up-to-date data. However, it can also be more resource-intensive, as it requires nodes to wait for a response from other nodes before continuing with their own operations.\\n \\n\\n Achieving consistency in a distributed system can be challenging for several reasons:\\n \\n\\n 1. Network latency: In a distributed system, there may be a delay between the time when data is updated on one node and when it is replicated to other nodes. This delay can lead to inconsistencies in the system, as different nodes may have different versions of the data.\\n \\n\\n 2. Node failures: In a distributed system, node failures can lead to data loss or inconsistencies in the system. If a node fails to replicate data to other nodes, the data may become out-of-date or lost entirely.\\n \\n\\n 3. Concurrent updates: In a distributed system, multiple nodes may be updating the same data at the same time. This can lead to conflicts and inconsistencies in the system, as different nodes may have different versions of the data.\\n \\n\\n 4. Lack of coordination: In a distributed system, nodes may not have a centralized authority to coordinate data updates and ensure consistency. This can lead to inconsistencies and conflicts between nodes, as each node may have its own understanding of the data and its own rules for updating it.\\n \\n\\n To address these challenges, distributed systems often use various techniques to ensure consistency, such as:\\n \\n\\n 1. Consistency models: Consistency models define the rules for how data is updated and accessed in a distributed system. There are several consistency models, including strong consistency (where all nodes have the same version of the data at all times), eventual consistency (where data eventually becomes consistent after updates are made), and causal consistency (where updates are made in a causal order, ensuring that the effects of one update are visible to all nodes before the effects of another update).\\n \\n\\n 2. Conflict resolution: Conflict resolution techniques are used to resolve conflicts between nodes when they are updating the same data. Techniques such as optimistic concurrency and pessimistic concurrency can be used to ensure that conflicts are resolved in a consistent and efficient manner.\\n \\n\\n 3. Replication strategies: Replication strategies are used to ensure that data is replicated to all nodes in the system in a consistent and efficient manner. Techniques such as master-slave replication, peer-to-peer replication, and asynchronous replication can be used to achieve different levels of consistency and efficiency in the system.\\n \\n\\n 4. Consistency protocols: Consistency protocols are used to ensure that nodes in the system have the same understanding of the data and its updates. Techniques such as two-phase commit and consensus algorithms can be used to ensure that all nodes in the system agree on the state of the data and its updates.\\n \\n\\n 5. Monitoring and logging: Monitoring and logging can be used to track the state of the data in the system and identify any inconsistencies or conflicts that may arise. Techniques such as logging and tracing can be used to track the history of data updates and ensure that all nodes in the system have the same understanding of the data.\\n \\n\\n 6. Testing and validation: Testing and validation can be used to ensure that the distributed system is functioning correctly and that data is being replicated in a consistent and efficient manner. Techniques such as unit testing, integration testing, and performance testing can be used to test the system and ensure that it is functioning as expected.\\n \\n\\n Achieving consistency in a distributed system requires a careful balance between consistency and availability. Too much consistency can lead to reduced availability, as nodes may be unable to update the data in a timely manner due to the need for coordination and consistency checks. Too little consistency can lead to data inconsistencies and conflicts, which can result in data loss or incorrect results. Therefore, it is important to carefully consider the consistency requirements of the system and choose the appropriate consistency model, replication strategy, and consistency protocol to ensure that the system meets those requirements while maintaining a high level of availability.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/706", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I need an audit report that includes 8 sections for a scenario, the sections include:\\n\\nSection 1: Purpose and scope\\nSection 2: Objectives\\nSection 3: Constraints\\nExamples of constraints:\\n- Time constraints\\n- Third party access constraints\\n- Business operations continuity constraints\\n- Scope of audit engagement\\n- Technology tools constraints\\n\\nSection 4: Components and Definitions\\nSection 5: Auditing Phases\\nSection 6: Auditing Tasks\\nIncludes the following tasks :\\nNetwork Scanning\\nVulnerability Scanning\\nPassword Cracking\\nLog Review\\nFile Integrity Check\\nVirus Detectors\\nWireless N/W Testing\\nAuthentication\\nSession Management\\nAccess control\\nCommunication security\\nBusiness Logic\\nBackup Storage\\nDisaster Recovery plan Implementation\\nConfiguration Documentation\\n\\nSection 7: Audit Methodologies\\nIncludes these:\\n–\\tRisk assessments\\n–\\tPolicy assessment\\n–\\tSocial engineering\\n–\\tSecurity design review\\n–\\tSecurity process review\\n–\\tInterviews\\n–\\tObservation\\n–\\tDocument review\\n–\\tTechnical review\\n\\nSection 8: Audit Report\\n\\nCan you do it?\", \"response\": \"Yes, I can do it. However, it would be helpful if you could provide more context about the scenario and the organization being audited. This information will help me create an audit report that is tailored to the specific needs and requirements of the organization. Here are the steps I would follow to create the audit report:\\n\\n1. Purpose and scope: This section should provide an overview of the purpose of the audit and the scope of the assessment. It should include information about the objectives of the audit, the scope of the assessment, and any constraints or limitations that may impact the audit process.\\n\\n2. Objectives: This section should outline the specific objectives of the audit, including the key areas that will be assessed and the goals that the audit is intended to achieve. The objectives should be aligned with the overall goals and objectives of the organization being audited.\\n\\n3. Constraints: This section should outline any constraints or limitations that may impact the audit process. This could include time constraints, third-party access constraints, business operations continuity constraints, scope of audit engagement, or technology tools constraints. By identifying these constraints upfront, the audit team can develop a plan to address them and ensure that the audit is conducted in a timely and effective manner.\\n\\n4. Components and definitions: This section should provide a detailed overview of the components and definitions that will be used throughout the audit process. This includes a description of the various components of the information technology infrastructure that will be assessed, as well as a definition of key terms and concepts that will be used throughout the audit report.\\n\\n5. Auditing phases: This section should outline the various phases of the audit process, including the planning phase, data collection phase, analysis phase, and reporting phase. It should also include a timeline for each phase, as well as a description of the activities that will be performed during each phase.\\n\\n6. Auditing tasks: This section should provide a detailed description of the specific tasks that will be performed during the audit process. This includes a description of the techniques and tools that will be used to perform each task, as well as a description of the expected results and the criteria that will be used to evaluate the results.\\n\\n7. Audit methodologies: This section should provide an overview of the audit methodologies that will be used during the audit process. This includes a description of the risk assessment methodology that will be used to identify and prioritize risks, as well as a description of the policy assessment methodology that will be used to evaluate the organization's information security policies and procedures. It should also include a description of the social engineering methodology that will be used to test the organization's security awareness and training programs, as well as a description of the security design review methodology that will be used to evaluate the organization's information security architecture and design.\\n\\n8. Audit report: This section should provide a detailed summary of the findings and recommendations from the audit process. It should include a description of the key risks and vulnerabilities that were identified during the audit process, as well as a description of the recommended actions that the organization should take to address these risks and vulnerabilities. The audit report should also include a summary of the audit methodology and a description of the results of each task performed during the audit process. Finally, the audit report should include a list of the key stakeholders who will receive the report, as well as a timeline for implementing the recommended actions.\\n\\nIn order to create an effective audit report, it is important to have a clear understanding of the organization's information technology infrastructure, as well as the specific objectives and constraints of the audit. By following the steps outlined above, you can create an audit report that is tailored to the specific needs and requirements of the organization, and that provides a comprehensive and accurate assessment of the organization's information security posture.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/360", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is information overload?\", \"response\": \"Information overload is a term used to describe the phenomenon of being bombarded with too much information, to the point where it becomes difficult to process and understand it all. It can occur in a variety of settings, such as in the workplace, at school, or even in our personal lives.\\n\\nThe term is often used in the context of technology, where the rapid advancement of information and communication technologies has led to an increase in the amount of information we are exposed to on a daily basis. This can include emails, social media notifications, news updates, and other forms of digital communication.\\n\\nInformation overload can have a number of negative effects, including stress, anxiety, and even physical health problems. It can also lead to a decrease in productivity and an increase in errors, as we struggle to keep up with the volume of information we are receiving.\\n\\nTo combat information overload, it's important to develop strategies for managing our information intake. This can include setting boundaries around our use of technology, taking regular breaks from screens, and practicing digital minimalism. It's also important to prioritize the information that is most important to us and to focus on quality over quantity.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/953", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"(text from:https://www.prosci.com/solutions/training-programs/change-management-certification-program) how many people has prosci certified?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nMore than 35,000 change management professionals have been certified by Prosci since the certification program began in 2003.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nacording to (text from:https://www.prosci.com/solutions/training-programs/change-management-certification-program) how much was the revenue made by prosci in their certification program?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nProsci has made more than $60 million in revenue from its change management certification program since its launch in 2003.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhats the cost of teh certification program?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe cost of the Prosci change management certification program varies depending on the program you choose, but generally ranges from $1,495 to $4,995.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nassume taht all teh studants made the cheaper program, and that the price hasn't changed over the yearshow much money rposci made since the start\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAssuming that all 35,000 change management professionals who have been certified by Prosci made the cheaper program, and that the price has remained the same over the years, Prosci would have made approximately $82 million since the certification program began in 2003.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nplease check (text from:https://www.prosci.com/solutions/training-programs/change-management-certification-program)\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I have just checked and confirmed that the revenue figure is correct, as reported in the above referenced source. This figure was verified as accurate on January 20, 2020.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow many students graduated\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIn 2018, a total of 2,164 students graduated from the Prosci Change Management Certification Program. These figures are updated annually.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhats teh cost of the program?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe Prosci Change Management Certification Program costs $1,495 per participant, or $1,995 per participant for a comprehensive, 3-day program. This price was verified as accurate on January 20, 2020.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat was teh revenue?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nDuring the 2018 calendar year, Prosci generated $13.8 million in revenue from its certification program. This figure was verified as accurate on January 20, 2020.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nassume that all did the 4900 program\", \"response\": \"Assuming that all 2,164 students who graduated from the Prosci Change Management Certification Program in 2018 enrolled in the more expensive, comprehensive 3-day program that costs $1,995 per participant, the total revenue generated would be:\\n \\n\\n Total revenue = Number of participants x Program cost\\n Total revenue = 2,164 x $1,995\\n Total revenue = $4,291,960\\n \\n\\n Therefore, Prosci generated approximately $4.3 million in revenue from its certification program in 2018, based on the assumption that all participants enrolled in the more expensive program.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/97", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"have you heard of amplitude?\", \"response\": \"Yes, I have heard of amplitude. In physics and engineering, amplitude is a measure of the strength of a wave or signal. It is the maximum displacement of a wave from its resting position or the maximum value of a signal. Amplitude is usually expressed in units of distance or voltage, and it is an important characteristic of a wave or signal that can affect its behavior and properties.\\n\\nIn particular, the amplitude of a wave can affect its energy, loudness, or intensity, depending on the context. In electronic circuits, the amplitude of a signal can be controlled by an amplifier or other components to achieve the desired level of output power or signal strength.\\n\\nAmplitude is a fundamental concept in many fields, including physics, engineering, electronics, and signal processing, and it has numerous practical applications in areas such as communication, navigation, and data transmission.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/1", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"explain master slave replication nsql\", \"response\": \"In SQL, master-slave replication is a technique used to create a copy of a database on a separate server. The master server is the primary server that contains the original data, while the slave server is the secondary server that contains a copy of the data. The master server sends updates to the slave server, which then applies them to its own database.\\n\\nHere's how master-slave replication works:\\n\\n1. The master server sends a stream of updates to the slave server, which includes information about changes made to the database on the master server.\\n\\n2. The slave server receives the updates and applies them to its own database, creating a copy of the master server's database.\\n\\n3. The slave server can also send updates back to the master server, which can be used to keep the two databases in sync. This is known as two-way replication.\\n\\n4. If the master server fails, the slave server can take over as the new master server, ensuring that the database remains available.\\n\\nMaster-slave replication can be used to increase the availability and scalability of a database, as well as to create a backup of the data in case of failure. However, it's important to note that master-slave replication can be complex to set up and maintain, and it may not be suitable for all types of databases.\\n\\nIn NoSQL, master-slave replication is similar to SQL in that it involves creating a copy of a database on a separate server. However, NoSQL databases are typically more flexible and scalable than SQL databases, and they may use different replication techniques.\\n\\nFor example, some NoSQL databases use a distributed architecture, where data is stored across multiple servers and replicated in real-time. This can provide high availability and fault tolerance, as well as increased performance.\\n\\nOther NoSQL databases may use a master-slave replication model similar to SQL, where a master server sends updates to one or more slave servers. However, NoSQL databases may also use other replication techniques, such as peer-to-peer replication or multi-master replication, depending on the specific needs of the application.\\n\\nOverall, master-slave replication is an important technique for creating a copy of a database on a separate server, increasing the availability and scalability of the database, and providing a backup in case of failure. While it can be complex to set up and maintain, it can be a valuable tool for ensuring the reliability and performance of a database.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/156", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a script for a tv series called \\\"the white lotus\\\" about six friends, laure, juan, sam, sandy, joost, and ryan, who are staying at a luxury hotel on an island off the coast of italy, and one of them is secretly a murderer\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s the rough outline of a script for a TV series called “The White Lotus”, about six friends, Laure, Juan, Sam, Sandy, Joost, and Ryan, who are staying at a luxury hotel on an island off the coast of Italy. One of them is secretly a murderer:\\n \\n\\n Laure, Juan, Sam, Sandy, Joost, and Ryan are staying at a luxury hotel on the Italian island of Ischia, when one of them is secretly a murderer. The rest of the group is largely unaware of this, and spends their time sunbathing, swimming, and eating at the hotel restaurant. The murderer uses various means to try to cover up their crime, but eventually the truth is revealed and the murderer is arrested.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nmake it more like the tv series \\\"the white lotus\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s a revised version that’s more in line with the style of the TV series “The White Lotus”:\\n \\n\\n Laure, Juan, Sam, Sandy, Joost, and Ryan are staying at a luxury hotel on the Italian island of Ischia, when one of them is secretly a murderer. The rest of the group is largely unaware of this, and spends their time sunbathing, swimming, and eating at the hotel restaurant. The murderer uses various means to try to cover up their crime, but eventually the truth is revealed and the murderer is arrested. However, the revelation of the murder creates a deep rift in the group, and the rest of the season follows the aftermath of the crime and the group’s struggle to recover.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nremove the last part and make it a full script\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s a revised version that ends at the revelation of the murder, making it a full script:\\n \\n\\n Laure, Juan, Sam, Sandy, Joost, and Ryan are staying at a luxury hotel on the Italian island of Ischia, when one of them is secretly a murderer. The rest of the group is largely unaware of this, and spends their time sunbathing, swimming, and eating at the hotel restaurant. The murderer uses various means to try to cover up their crime, but eventually the truth is revealed and the murderer is arrested.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nmake it shorter and more mysterious\", \"response\": \"Here’s a revised version that’s shorter and more mysterious:\\n \\n\\n Laure, Juan, Sam, Sandy, Joost, and Ryan are staying at a luxury hotel on the Italian island of Ischia, when one of them is secretly a murderer. The rest of the group is largely unaware of this, and spends their time sunbathing, swimming, and eating at the hotel restaurant. The murderer uses various means to try to cover up their crime, but eventually the truth is revealed and the murderer is arrested. However, the revelation of the murder creates a deep rift in the group, and the rest of the season follows the aftermath of the crime and the group’s struggle to recover.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"l